cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  60-degree-free subsets of the Leech minimal vectors, and kissing
  numbers in dimensions 25-31
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lindow
    given-names: Ben
abstract: >-
  A computational study of the maximum size of a subset S of the 196560
  minimal vectors of the Leech lattice in which no two members subtend an
  angle of exactly 60 degrees, and of the structure of the largest known
  examples. Such sets drive the best known kissing-number lower bounds in
  dimensions 25 through 31. Includes a new lower bound K(27) >= 200540, a
  certified ladder 496 <= max|S| <= 837 whose upper end is a three-point
  semidefinite program with an exact-rational dual certificate, at least 64
  pairwise Co_0-inequivalent maximal 496-element sets, and a structural
  account of those sets in terms of a Turyn decomposition.
keywords:
  - kissing number
  - Leech lattice
  - spherical codes
  - independent set
  - semidefinite programming
  - association scheme
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/btlindow/KissingNumbers'
year: 2026
date-released: '2026-09-01'
